{#
    User badges - Floating badge strip pinned to the user card avatar

    Renders one round chip per badge in the top-right corner of the nearest positioned
    ancestor (the usercard's .card-image). Chips lay out side by side, so an additional
    badge provider appends without any layout change. Each chip carries a CSS tooltip with
    the badge's translated meaning plus a screen-reader-only copy of the same text, and
    the whole strip is skipped when the user has no badges.

    Used in:    templates/_components/usercard.html.twig
    Parameters:
        - badges (UserBadge[], required) - list of UserBadge DTOs with color, icon, and
                                           title, where title is a translation key
    Depends on: .has-tooltip and .usercard-badges in assets/styles/custom.scss
#}
{% if badges is not empty %}
    <div class="usercard-badges">
        {% for badge in badges %}
            {% set label = badge.title|trans %}
            <span class="usercard-badge has-tooltip has-tooltip-end {{ badge.color }}" data-tooltip="{{ label }}">
                <i class="{{ badge.icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="is-sr-only">{{ label }}</span>
            </span>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
